# The multi-Vt pack recipe (examples/mvt-mini/abc/mvt.abc: both &nf calls load-aware,
# {period} = the flow's clock period in ps, &deepsyn bounded by -J steps without
# improvement, no wall-clock -T, so the result is reproducible; the -J, -I and -S
# values are an example, not a tuned setting) plus ONE added line: after &deepsyn,
#     &sopb; &b -d
# (SOP balancing, then delay-only AIG balancing). &deepsyn, dc2 and scorr minimise
# area and are blind to depth: they fold a parallel-prefix adder back into a
# near-ripple chain, so the deepest cone of a design can end up much deeper
# than the subject graph CombToSynth built. &sopb/&b -d re-balance the AIG for
# delay before the final &nf mapping, which costs some area.
# Use with: --abc-script-file recipes/depth_recovery.abc  (or flow.abc_script_file)
strash; scorr; dc2
&get -n; &deepsyn -J 20 -I 4 -S 200; &put
strash; &get -n; &sopb; &b -d; &put
strash; &get -n; &dch -f; &if -C 32 -K 6; &put
strash; &get -n; &resub -N 2; &put
resub -K 16 -N 3
strash; &get -n; &dch -f; &nf -l -C 32 -D {period}; &put
strash; &get -n; &nf -l -D {period}; &put
